menu "LagunBus — key"

config LAGUN_TWAI_TX
    int "TWAI transmit GPIO"
    default 4
    help
        4 and 5 by default, because on the ESP32-C3 Super Mini they are broken out
        and play no other role. AVOID 2, 8 and 9 — those are boot-mode strapping
        pins, and their state at reset decides whether the board starts at all.
        Avoid 18 and 19 too: USB Serial/JTAG goes that way, that is, flashing and
        the log.

config LAGUN_TWAI_RX
    int "TWAI receive GPIO"
    default 5

config LAGUN_KEY_GPIO
    int "Key GPIO"
    default 3
    help
        A key shorting to ground, with the internal pull-up. The resting state is
        then high, and main.c reads a LOW pin as a press.

config LAGUN_BITRATE
    int "Bus speed [bit/s]"
    default 500000
    help
        Has to agree with the hub and with EVERY other node. A node at a different
        speed not only hears nobody — it corrupts frames for all the others.

endmenu
